  "properties": {
    "title": "Cropping intensity",
    "description": "Cropping intensity map for India. Cropping intensity is computed on the IndiaSAT Land Use Land Cover outputs by taking the weighted average of the area under single cropping, double cropping, and tripple/annual/perennial cropping. The vector map is available from 2017 onwards.Details of methodology can be found in the technical manual and the codebase on [github](https://github.com/core-stack-org/core-stack-backend/tree/main/computing/cropping_intensity).",
